      "writtenOn": "2021-02-25T12:18:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let me see if I understand this correctly: we have a [][]interface{}\n\n- The outer index chooses which property struct we are talking about\n- The inner index chooses which arch we are talking about (if I read createArchPropTypeDesc line 798 correctly)\n- and the interface{} is actually an archPropRoot (line 953)\n- each member (Arch/Multilib/Target) of archPropRoot is a dummy value of an unnamed struct type created at runtime (line 831) that has only the fields that are specific to each architecture / target / multilib, whatever the latter is\n\nMaybe this is worth adding a comment?\n\n(the code is fine, I just want to make sure that I understand this correctly)",
